To check if an app is compatible with a specific iOS version, you can use the `System.getProperty("os.name").equals("Mac OS X")` method in Java.

Here's how you can do it:

```java
import java.lang.System;

public class AppVersion {
    public static boolean isAppCompatible(String minOs, String targetOs) {
        if (minOs.equals(targetOs)) {
            return true;
        }

        // Check for iOS versions using the system property "os.version"
        String osName = System.getProperty("os.name");
        String osVersion = System.getProperty("os.version");

        int minOsInt = Integer.parseInt(minOs.split("-")[0]);
        int targetOsInt = Integer.parseInt(targetOs.split("-")[0]);

        if (osName.equals("Mac OS X") && osVersion.startsWith(targetOs.split("-")[0])) {
            return true;
        }

        return false;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
